="journal">Hirono-Hara, Y., H. Noji, M. Nishiura, E. Muneyuki, K. Y. Hara, R. Yasuda, K. Kinosita Jr., and M. Yoshida. <year>2001</year>. Pause and rotation of F<sub>1</sub>-ATPase during catalysis. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>13649</fpage>&#x02013;13654.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11707579</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Noji, H., R. Yasuda, M. Yoshida, and K. Kinosita Jr. <year>1997</year>. Direct observation of the rotation of F<sub>1</sub>-ATPase. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>386</volume>:<fpage>299</fpage>&#x02013;302.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9069291</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yasuda, R., H. Noji, K. Kinosita Jr., and M. Yoshida. <year>1998</year>. F<sub>1</sub>-ATPase is a highly efficient molecular motor that rotates with discrete 120&#x000b0; steps. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>93</volume>:<fpage>1117</fpage>&#x02013;1124.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9657145</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Adachi, K., R. Yasuda, H. Noji, H. Itoh, Y. Harada, M. Yoshida, and K. Kinosita Jr. <year>2000</year>. Stepping rotation of F<sub>1</sub>-ATPase visualized through angle-resolved single-fluorophore imaging. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>97</volume>:<fpage>7243</fpage>&#x02013;7247.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10840052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yasuda, R., H. Noji, M. Yoshida, K. Kinosita Jr., and H. Itoh. <year>2001</year>. Resolution of distinct rotational substeps by submillisecond kinetic analysis of F<sub>1</sub>-ATPase. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>410</volume>:<fpage>898</fpage>&#x02013;904.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11309608</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Adachi, K., K. Oiwa, T. Nis